<p style="max-width:990px; padding-top:15px">'''MLBB Mid Season Cup''', also known as '''MSC''', is a Mid-Season international championship, replacing the previous [[MSC|MLBB Southeast Asia Cup]]. It now stands as the second international in-season major.

The 2026 edition was announced as part of the '''Esports World Cup''' game titles line-up on January 21, 2026, and the entire MSC branding received a total visual design rebranding for this edition. It was originally planned to be hosted in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, but was moved to Paris, France on May 20.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/EWC_EN/status/2057121960623006162|title=Esports World Cup 2026 is coming to Paris|author=Esports World Cup|author-link=Esports World Cup|date=2026-05-20}}</ref> <br> <br>

[[Team Spirit]] defeated [[Yangon Galacticos]] by a scoreline of 4–3 at the grand final, becoming the first Western team to ever win a major championship, with all previous major titles having been taken by Southeast Asian teams. <br> <br>

On August 7, 2026, Moonton introduced the '''Title Defender''' mechanism for MSC 2027.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/mlbbesports_en/status/2085677093170585780|title=Introducing "Title Defender" For MSC 2027.|author=MLBB Esports|date=2026-08-07}}</ref> [[Team Spirit]] earns an automatic Main Stage berth at MSC 2027, while [[Yangon Galacticos]] is granted a Wildcard or equivalent entry. In case a team qualifies for the Main Stage slot through the regional qualifier then the slot will be passed to the next seeded team.
:''See [https://liquipedia.net/esports/Esports_World_Cup/2026 here] to read about the Esports World Cup 2026, the Calendar, the Club Standings and more.''
</p>

