==Format==
''All stages are played at {{flag|fr}} Paris Expo Porte de Versailles''
<section begin="WCFormat"/>* All matches will be played with {{AMC}}
* '''Wildcard:''' ''July 1st - 4th, 2026 at {{flag|fr}} Qiddiya Battleground (Backstage)''
** '''''Wildcard stage will be played backstage with no crowd attendance
** Group Stage
*** 10 teams split into 2 groups of 5
*** Single round-robin, all matches are played in {{Abbr/Bo1}}
*** {{bgcolortext|seedup|{{Ordinal|1|sup=yes}} placed teams}} from each group are seeded directly into the Decider Stage
*** {{bgcolortext|up|{{Ordinal|2|sup=yes}} to {{Ordinal|4|sup=yes}} placed teams}} from each group advance to the Gauntlet Stage
*** {{bgcolortext|down|{{Ordinal|5|sup=yes}} placed teams}} from each group are eliminated
***<span class="mw-customtoggle-Tiebreaker" style="border-bottom:1px dotted;">''Click here to know the '''Wildcard''' tiebreaker rules''</span>
<div class="toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" id="mw-customcollapsible-Tiebreaker" style="width:760px; margin-left:45px">
If somehow 2 or 3 teams have the same score, there will be tiebreaker to decide the ranking
* '''2-way Tiebreaker'''
** Upper position will be decided by previous head to head.
* '''3-way Tiebreaker'''
** Upper position will be decided by head to head Match record with teams involved
** Upper position will be decided games diff.
** If Games Diff cannot determine the rankings of 3 teams involved, Additional match will be applied
*** The three teams will play two additional games according to the ranking of winning time of the first-round tiebreaker. The fastest game win of three teams will be sorted in ascending order.
***'''Example:'''
****Team 1 - 10:00
****Team 2 - 11:00
****Team 3 - 12:00
***Teams 2 and 3 will play a {{abbr/Bo1}} match and the winner will face Team 1 in a {{abbr/Bo1}} match.
***The winner between Team 1 and Team 2 or 3 will get the upper position.
** If Games Diff cannot determine the rankings of 2 teams involved, Additional match will be applied
***The Match will be {{Abbr/Bo1}}
***The winner will get the upper position.
</div> 
** Gauntlet Stage
*** Two separate King-of-the-Hill brackets, all matches are played in {{Abbr/Bo3}}
*** The two {{bgcolortext|stayup|{{Ordinal|4|sup=yes}} placed teams}} face the {{bgcolortext|stayup|{{Ordinal|3|sup=yes}} placed teams}} from the other group; the winner challenges the {{bgcolortext|up|{{Ordinal|2|sup=yes}} placed team}}
*** {{bgcolortext|up|The top team of each gauntlet}} advances to the Decider Stage
** Decider Stage
*** Single-elimination bracket, all matches are played in {{Abbr/Bo3}}
*** {{bgcolortext|seedup|Top team of Group A}} first plays the winner of Gauntlet B; {{bgcolortext|seedup|top team of Group B}} first plays the winner of Gauntlet A
*** {{bgcolortext|up|The winner}} between the two remaining teams qualifies to the '''[[MSC/2026/Group Stage|Group Stage]]'''
**<section end="WCFormat"/>
<section begin="GSFormat"/>* '''Group Stage:''' ''July 22nd - 26th, 2026 at {{flag|fr}} Lenovo Legion Gauntlet (Arena)''
** 16 teams split into 2 groups of 8
** Two double-elimination (GSL) brackets, all matches are played in {{Abbr/Bo3}}
** {{bgcolortext|up|Top 4 teams}} from each group advance to '''[[MSC/2026/Knockout Stage|Knockout Stage]]'''
** {{bgcolortext|down|Remaining 4 teams}} from each group are eliminated<section end="GSFormat"/>
<section begin="PLFormat"/>* '''Knockout Stage:''' ''July 29th - August 1st, 2026 at {{flag|fr}} Lenovo Legion Gauntlet (Arena)''
** Single-elimination bracket
** Each 2-0 team selects their opponent from the pool of 2-1 teams
*** Picking order is determined by point differential (game wins - game losses) in the Group Stage
*** In case of ties, the following tiebreakers are applied in order:
**** Lowest total winning time
**** Fastest match victory
**** Slowest match victory
**** Fastest individual game
**** Slowest individual game
**** Random draw, if still tied
** Grand Final is played in {{Abbr/Bo7}}, all other matches are played in {{Abbr/Bo5}}<section end="PLFormat"/>

